    "narrative": "Our offensive focus for May 14th centers on capitalizing on the favorable matchup against McGreevy, making **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91) our undisputed primary play. His high score is bolstered by a potent combination of a 10% park factor, a 9% SP skill boost, and a clean #3 spot in the order, positioning him to maximize run production. **Brice Turang** (63.20) and **Josh Naylor** (62.00) round out our elite Tier-1 starts; **Brice Turang** benefits significantly from hitting #2 against Canning, while **Josh Naylor** capitalizes on a strong order slot and a favorable dynamic platoon advantage. While **James Wood** only slots in at 55.32, his aggressive #1 spot in the order, combined with favorable wind conditions and a solid xwOBA, keeps him firmly in the lineup despite a tough matchup against Burns.\n\nWe are navigating a treacherous slate against several elite arms, most notably Chris Sale and Jes\u00fas Luzardo. Consequently, the scoring profile for **Seiya Suzuki** (46.31) and **Trevor Story** (45.72) is suppressed by SP difficulty, necessitating careful monitoring of their \"Lineup Pending\" status to ensure they aren't pushed further down the order. The most difficult bench decision involved **Cole Young**, who fell just short of our 40.0 \"Zebras\" floor with a 39.51 score. Despite his potential, his #9 spot in the order and a poor dynamic platoon matchup against Burrows rendered him a liability compared to the higher efficiency ratings of **Vinnie Pasquantino** (57.00) and **Henry Bolte** (56.72). \n\nWe are largely avoiding high-risk, low-reward scenarios today, as evidenced by the decision to sit **Mickey Moniak** (39.28) and **Zach McKinstry** (33.97). While we remain aggressive in chasing stolen bases, our rostered speed threats like **Corbin Carroll** are inactive today, placing the burden of production on our high-efficiency hitters against softer matchups. Be advised: with several players including **Dalton Rushing**, **Austin Riley**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Vinnie Pasquantino** waiting on pending lineups, we must be ready to pivot if tactical adjustments by managers force them into bottom-third lineup slots, which would further erode their daily efficiency scores.",
